\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces Walk correction and DRUP. Panel A: matched configurations, DRUP minus DR adjacency at the same configuration, for each value of $\beta $ in the grid, on the real data. Mean differences are $\times 10^{-3}$ nDCG@5; ``share $<0$'' is the fraction of the matched configurations with a negative mean test difference (1{,}440 on Coat, 512 on Yahoo! R3); ``splits $<0$'' counts the splits in which the mean over configurations is negative. Panel B: validated score ensemble $s=(1-w)\,z(A)+w\,z(\mathrm  {DRUP})$, with $z$ standardisation over unlogged items and $w$ chosen per split on validation data; A is the final method. Holm family of 11 tests within each dataset.}}{42}{table.9}\protected@file@percent }
